/-!
# The residual ideal sheaf of a blowup is supported at finitely many closed points

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a two-dimensional regular local ring with `𝔪 = (x, y)`, let `X` be the blowup of
`Spec A` at its closed point with exceptional divisor `E`, and let `L` be an ideal of `A` with
`𝔪 ^ n ⊆ L ⊆ 𝔪` for some `n`. This file proves the first half of [Stacks, Tag 0AGT]: the inverse
image `L·𝒪_X` factors as

`L·𝒪_X = 𝒪_X(-dE)·ℐ'`

for a positive integer `d` and a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf `ℐ'` whose support consists of
finitely many closed points of `X`, each of codimension two — the points `x₁, …, x_r` at which
`𝒪_X/ℐ'` of that tag is supported.

## The argument

`E` is an effective Cartier divisor ([Stacks, Tag 02OS]) and its support is nonempty, so among
the exponents `e` with `L·𝒪_X ⊆ 𝒪_X(-eE)` there is a largest one, `d`
(`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.exists_maximal_order`); it is positive because
`L ⊆ 𝔪`. Dividing by the effective Cartier divisor `dE`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mul_eq_of_le_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`) produces the cofactor `ℐ'`.

What remains is to see that `ℐ'` is *residual* on each of the two standard charts `A[𝔪/x]` and
`A[𝔪/y]` covering `X`: on the chart of a generator `a`, writing `ξ` for the image of `a` — the
local equation of `E` there — the ideal of `ℐ'` contains a power of `ξ` and is not contained in
`(ξ)`. The first is immediate from `𝔪 ^ n ⊆ L`, since `ξ ^ d` is a nonzerodivisor which is not a
unit. The second is the only point where the two charts talk to each other, and it is settled
here without comparing them: were the ideal of `ℐ'` contained in `(ξ)` on *one* chart, the
contraction computation `(ξ ^ k)·A[𝔪/a] ∩ A = 𝔪 ^ k` of this file would give `L ⊆ 𝔪 ^ (d + 1)`
and hence `L·𝒪_X ⊆ 𝒪_X(-(d+1)E)`, contradicting the maximality of `d`. So the order of `L·𝒪_X`
along `E` is visible on either chart alone.

Given that, the primes of a chart containing a residual ideal are finitely many, maximal, and of
height two, by the sibling module `CartierDescent.ChartResidualSupport`. Those three facts are
read off at points of `X` through the affine dictionary of `CartierDescent.AffineIdealSheaf`, and
closedness in `X` — rather than merely in a chart — follows because a point of the support that
specializes to a point of a chart lies in that same chart, open sets being stable under
generization, and is maximal there.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.exists_residual_isEffectiveCartier_support`: the
  finite support assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0AGT].

## Implementation notes

The blowup is `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)` throughout, the construction carrying the
affine-chart API, so the effective Cartier divisor input is
`Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal_reesData` rather than the statement for
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`; transporting the conclusion along `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpIso` is left to
the consumer.

The base ring of both charts is `Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`, not `A`, since that is where the sections of the
centre live. All the hypotheses needed of it — regular local of dimension two, hence a Noetherian
domain, with maximal ideal generated by the images of `x` and `y` — are transported along
`Scheme.ΓSpecIso` by `IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv` and `ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv`, so the
chart statements of the sibling modules apply verbatim with that ring in place of `A`.

Two shapes of statement are kept apart on purpose. Everything whose statement mentions the blowup
is assembled from terms whose types are inferred, never by `rw` or `simp` on an assembled goal:
as the implementation notes of `CartierDescent.SurfaceCharts` record, a single rewrite whose rule
must be matched against a goal mentioning both the blowup and an `Ideal.map` through
`Γ(Spec ·, ⊤)` exhausts the heartbeat budget. Everything else — the ring theory, and the passage
from primes of a chart to points of a scheme — is stated with the scheme, the ring, or the ideals
behind variables, where tactics are cheap; the chart generator `a` is likewise kept as a variable
rather than substituted by the image of `x`, which is what keeps the two chart lemmas inside the
budget.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent

/-! ### Dividing a power of the maximal ideal by a regular parameter -/

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]

/-- The first element of a regular sequence acts injectively. -/
private lemma isSMulRegular_of_isRegular {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y]) : IsSMulRegular R x := by
  rw [RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_cons_iff] at hreg
  exact hreg.1

/-- **Dividing a power of the maximal ideal by one parameter**: `𝔪 ^ (j + 1) : x ⊆ 𝔪 ^ j` for
`x` the first member of a regular sequence `x, y` spanning `𝔪`.

Writing `𝔪 ^ (j + 2) = x·𝔪 ^ (j + 1) + y·𝔪 ^ (j + 1)` and `a x = u x + v y`, the element `v y`
is divisible by `x`, hence so is `v`; cancelling `x` exhibits `a` as `u + w y` with
`w x = v ∈ 𝔪 ^ (j + 1)`, so that `w ∈ 𝔪 ^ j` by induction. -/
private lemma mem_pow_of_mul_mem_pow_succ {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R) (j : ℕ) {a : R}
    (h : a * x ∈ maximalIdeal R ^ (j + 1)) : a ∈ maximalIdeal R ^ j := by
  induction j generalizing a with
  | zero => simp [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
  | succ j ih =>
    have hy : y ∈ maximalIdeal R :=
      hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ rfl)
    have hsplit : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) =
        Ideal.span ({x} : Set R) ⊔ Ideal.span ({y} : Set R) :=
      Ideal.span_insert x {y}
    have hdecomp : maximalIdeal R ^ (j + 1 + 1) =
        maximalIdeal R ^ (j + 1) * Ideal.span ({x} : Set R) ⊔
          maximalIdeal R ^ (j + 1) * Ideal.span ({y} : Set R) := by
      rw [pow_succ, ← hspan, hsplit, Ideal.mul_sup]
    rw [hdecomp] at h
    obtain ⟨u', hu', v', hv', heq⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp h
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hux⟩ := Ideal.mem_mul_span_singleton.mp hu'
    obtain ⟨v, hv, hvy⟩ := Ideal.mem_mul_span_singleton.mp hv'
    have hvymem : v * y ∈ Ideal.span ({x} : Set R) :=
      Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨a - u, by rw [← hux, ← hvy] at heq; linear_combination -heq⟩
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ :=
      Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp (mem_span_singleton_of_mul_mem_span_singleton hreg v hvymem)
    have hwmem : w ∈ maximalIdeal R ^ j := ih (by rw [hw]; exact hv)
    have hax : x • a = x • (u + w * y) := by
      rw [← hux, ← hvy, ← hw] at heq
      simp only [smul_eq_mul]
      linear_combination -heq
    rw [isSMulRegular_of_isRegular hreg hax]
    exact Ideal.add_mem _ hu (by rw [pow_succ]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hwmem hy)

/-- **Dividing a power of the maximal ideal by a power of one parameter**:
`𝔪 ^ (N + k) : x ^ N ⊆ 𝔪 ^ k`, the iterate of
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.mem_pow_of_mul_mem_pow_succ`. -/
private lemma mem_pow_of_mul_pow_mem_pow {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R) (N k : ℕ) {a : R}
    (h : a * x ^ N ∈ maximalIdeal R ^ (N + k)) : a ∈ maximalIdeal R ^ k := by
  induction N generalizing a with
  | zero => simpa using h
  | succ N ih =>
    refine ih (mem_pow_of_mul_mem_pow_succ hreg hspan (N + k) ?_)
    rw [show a * x ^ N * x = a * x ^ (N + 1) by ring, show N + k + 1 = N + 1 + k by omega]
    exact h

/-! ### An element of the base divisible by a power of the denominator on a chart -/

/-- An element of `R` whose image in the chart `R[I/a]` is divisible by the `k`-th power of the
image of `a` satisfies `a ^ n z = a ^ k w` in `R`, for some `n` and some `w ∈ I ^ n`: the
divisibility is an equality of fractions with denominator a power of `a`, and `R` is a domain, so
the denominators can be cleared. -/
private lemma exists_mul_pow_eq_of_mem_span_pow [IsDomain R] (I : Ideal R) {a : R} (haI : a ∈ I)
    (ha : a ≠ 0) {z : R} {k : ℕ}
    (hz : algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) z ∈
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) a ^ k}) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (w : R), w ∈ I ^ n ∧ a ^ n * z = a ^ k * w := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hz
  obtain ⟨n, w, hw, hbw⟩ := (affineBlowup_mem_iff I a haI (b : Localization.Away a)).mp b.2
  refine ⟨n, w, hw, ?_⟩
  have hval : (b : Localization.Away a) * algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) a ^ k =
      algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) z := by
    have h := congrArg (Subalgebra.val (affineBlowup I a)) hb
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, AlgHom.commutes, AlgHom.commutes] at h
    exact h
  rw [hbw] at hval
  have hz' : (Localization.mk z (⟨a ^ 0, 0, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers a) : Localization.Away a) =
      Localization.mk (a ^ k * w) (⟨a ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers a) := by
    rw [show (⟨a ^ 0, 0, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers a) = 1 from Subtype.ext (pow_zero a),
      Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, ← hval,
      show (algebraMap R (Localization.Away a)) a ^ k =
        Localization.mk (a ^ k) 1 from by rw [Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, map_pow],
      Localization.mk_mul]
    congr 1
    · ring
    · exact Subtype.ext (by simp)
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := (affineBlowup_repr_eq_iff a 0 n z (a ^ k * w)).mp hz'
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp hj with h | h
  · exact absurd h (pow_ne_zero j ha)
  · exact sub_eq_zero.mp (by simpa using h)

/-- **The order of an ideal along the exceptional divisor is already visible on one chart.** If
the extension of `L` to the chart `R[𝔪/x]` is divisible by the `k`-th power of the image of `x`,
then `L ⊆ 𝔪 ^ k`.

This is what makes the order of `L·𝒪_X` along the exceptional divisor independent of the chart it
is read on: both charts see the order of `L` in the base. -/
private lemma le_pow_of_map_le_span_pow [IsDomain R] {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R)) (hx : x ≠ 0) (L : Ideal R) (k : ℕ)
    (hle : Ideal.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x)) L ≤
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x ^ k}) :
    L ≤ maximalIdeal R ^ k := by
  have hxm : x ∈ maximalIdeal R := hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert _ _)
  have hxI : x ∈ I := by rw [hI]; exact Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert _ _)
  intro z hz
  obtain ⟨m, w, hw, hzw⟩ :=
    exists_mul_pow_eq_of_mem_span_pow I hxI hx (hle (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hz))
  rw [hI, hspan] at hw
  refine mem_pow_of_mul_pow_mem_pow hreg hspan m k ?_
  rw [mul_comm, hzw, show m + k = k + m by omega, pow_add]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul (Ideal.pow_mem_pow hxm k) hw

/-- A regular nonunit `ξ`, a power of which lies in `Lc`, has a power in `Lc` once a power of it
lies in `(ξ ^ d)·Lc`: the factor can be cancelled, and the exponent cannot drop below `d`
because `ξ` is not invertible. -/
private lemma exists_pow_mem_of_pow_mem_span_mul {B : Type*} [CommRing B] {ξ : B}
    (hξ : ξ ∈ nonZeroDivisors B) (hnu : ¬ IsUnit ξ) {Lc : Ideal B} {m d : ℕ}
    (h : ξ ^ m ∈ Ideal.span {ξ ^ d} * Lc) : ∃ k : ℕ, ξ ^ k ∈ Lc := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hξc⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton_mul.mp h
  rcases le_or_gt d m with hdm | hmd
  · refine ⟨m - d, ?_⟩
    have hcancel : ξ ^ d * c = ξ ^ d * ξ ^ (m - d) := by
      rw [hξc, ← pow_add]
      congr 1
      omega
    rw [mul_cancel_left_mem_nonZeroDivisors (pow_mem hξ d)] at hcancel
    exact hcancel ▸ hc
  · exfalso
    refine hnu (isUnit_iff_dvd_one.mpr ⟨ξ ^ (d - m - 1) * c, ?_⟩)
    refine (mul_cancel_left_mem_nonZeroDivisors (pow_mem hξ m)).mp ?_
    have hgroup : ξ ^ m * (ξ * (ξ ^ (d - m - 1) * c)) = ξ ^ d * c := by
      rw [← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, ← pow_succ, ← pow_add]
      congr 2
      omega
    rw [mul_one, hgroup, hξc]

/-- A nonzero first member of a regular sequence: multiplication by `0` is injective only on the
zero ring. -/
private lemma ne_zero_of_isSMulRegular [Nontrivial R] {x : R} (h : IsSMulRegular R x) :
    x ≠ 0 := by
  rintro rfl
  exact one_ne_zero (h (show (0 : R) • (1 : R) = (0 : R) • (0 : R) by simp))

/-- **A pair generating the maximal ideal of a two-dimensional regular local ring is a regular
sequence**, by Stacks tag 00NQ: the pair is a minimal generating set, since the
`Submodule.spanFinrank` of the maximal ideal is the dimension. -/
public lemma isRegular_pair_of_span [IsRegularLocalRing R] (hdim : ringKrullDim R = 2)
    {x y : R} (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y] := by
  have hsf : (maximalIdeal R).spanFinrank = 2 := by
    have h := IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := R)
    rw [hdim] at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  have hofList : Ideal.ofList [x, y] = maximalIdeal R := by
    rw [← hspan, Ideal.ofList_cons, Ideal.ofList_cons, Ideal.ofList_nil]
    simp [Ideal.span_insert]
  exact ((IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay
    R).1 [x, y] hofList (by simp [hsf])).1

/-! ### The chart results with the centre in its ideal-sheaf spelling

The chart computations of the sibling module `CartierDescent.ChartResidualSupport`
are stated for the chart `affineBlowup (Ideal.span {x, y}) x`, while the chart of the blowup of an
ideal sheaf is the one of `(centre A).ideal ⊤`. The two ideals are equal, by
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.centre_ideal_top`, so each statement is repeated with
the ideal behind a variable and that equality as a hypothesis. -/

/-- `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.isPrime_span_algebraMap` with the centre's ideal
behind a variable. -/
public lemma isPrime_span_algebraMap' {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R)) :
    (Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x}).IsPrime := by
  subst hI
  exact isPrime_span_algebraMap R hreg hspan

/-- `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.not_isUnit_algebraMap_of_isRegular` with the
centre's ideal behind a variable. -/
public lemma not_isUnit_algebraMap' {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R)) :
    ¬ IsUnit (algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x) := by
  subst hI
  exact not_isUnit_algebraMap_of_isRegular R hreg hspan

/-- `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.finite_setOf_isPrime_le` with the centre's ideal
behind a variable. -/
public lemma finite_setOf_isPrime_le' [IsNoetherianRing R] {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R))
    (Lc : Ideal (affineBlowup I x)) (k : ℕ)
    (hxk : algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x ^ k ∈ Lc)
    (hL : ¬ Lc ≤ Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x}) :
    {p : Ideal (affineBlowup I x) | p.IsPrime ∧ Lc ≤ p}.Finite := by
  subst hI
  exact finite_setOf_isPrime_le R hreg hspan Lc k hxk hL

/-- `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.isMaximal_of_isPrime_le` with the centre's ideal
behind a variable. -/
public lemma isMaximal_of_isPrime_le' {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R))
    (Lc : Ideal (affineBlowup I x)) (k : ℕ)
    (hxk : algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x ^ k ∈ Lc)
    (hL : ¬ Lc ≤ Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x})
    {p : Ideal (affineBlowup I x)} (hp : p.IsPrime) (hLp : Lc ≤ p) : p.IsMaximal := by
  subst hI
  exact isMaximal_of_isPrime_le R hreg hspan Lc k hxk hL hp hLp

/-- `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.height_eq_two_of_lt` with the centre's ideal
behind a variable. -/
public lemma height_eq_two_of_lt' [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R] {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R))
    {p : Ideal (affineBlowup I x)} (hp : p.IsPrime)
    (hlt : Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x} < p) :
    ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime p) = 2 := by
  subst hI
  exact height_eq_two_of_lt R hreg hspan hp hlt

/-! ### The base of the charts: the sections of the structure sheaf over all of `Spec A` -/

/-- The sections of `𝒪_{Spec A}` over all of `Spec A` form a regular local ring when `A` does:
they are isomorphic to `A` through `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`. -/
public lemma isRegularLocalRing_sections (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] :
    IsRegularLocalRing Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) :=
  IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- The Krull dimension of the sections of `𝒪_{Spec A}` over all of `Spec A` is that of `A`. -/
public lemma ringKrullDim_sections (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    ringKrullDim Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) = ringKrullDim A :=
  ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- The maximal ideal of the sections of `𝒪_{Spec A}` over all of `Spec A` is the extension of
the maximal ideal of `A` along `ι : A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`. -/
private lemma map_inv_maximalIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsLocalRing Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)] :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) := by
  have hcomap : Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) =
      Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).hom.hom (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :=
    Ideal.map_comap_of_equiv
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  rw [hcomap]
  exact IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective _
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective)

/-- A pair spanning the maximal ideal of `A` spans the maximal ideal of `Γ(Spec A, ⊤)` after
transport along `ι : A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`. -/
public lemma span_pair_inv_eq_maximalIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsLocalRing Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)] {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    Ideal.span ({(Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom x,
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom y} : Set Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) := by
  rw [← map_inv_maximalIdeal A, ← hspan, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_pair]

/-! ### The residual ideal sheaf read on a chart -/

/-- `Ideal.map_map` with all three rings behind variables, so that it can be applied as a term to
an already-elaborated left-hand side instead of matched against a goal. -/
private lemma map_map_eq {R T V : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [CommRing V]
    (f : R →+* T) (g : T →+* V) (K : Ideal R) :
    Ideal.map g (Ideal.map f K) = Ideal.map (g.comp f) K :=
  Ideal.map_map f g

/-- **The sections of a product of inverse-image ideal sheaves over an affine target**,
transported along a ring map. Inverse image is multiplicative
(`Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_mul`), reading an ideal sheaf on an affine open is
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_mul`), and so is `Ideal.map`.

Both schemes are behind variables so that neither the blowup nor the spectrum of an affine blowup
algebra has to be unfolded while this step is checked. -/
@[ega "0 4.3.5" "special case"]
private lemma map_ideal_comap_mul_top {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] {T : Type u} [CommRing T]
    (f : Γ(Y, ⊤) →+* T) (P Q : X.IdealSheafData) (g : Y ⟶ X) :
    Ideal.map f (((P * Q).comap g).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.map f ((P.comap g).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) *
        Ideal.map f ((Q.comap g).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) :=
  (congrArg (Ideal.map f)
      ((congrArg (fun K : Y.IdealSheafData => K.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩)
            (Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_mul P Q g)).trans
        (congrFun (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_mul (I := P.comap g) (J := Q.comap g)) _))).trans
    (Ideal.map_mul f _ _)

/-- **The residual ideal sheaf read on a chart.** If `𝒪_X(-dE)·J' = L·𝒪_X` on the blowup `X` of
`Spec A` at its closed point, then on the chart `Spec A[𝔪/a]` attached to a section `a` of the
centre the ideal of `𝒪_X(-dE)` times the ideal of `J'` is `L·A[𝔪/a]`.

The first factor is `Ideal.span {ξ ^ d}` by
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal_pow`; it is left
unreduced here so that this equality can be assembled from terms whose types are inferred, never
by rewriting in a goal mentioning the blowup. -/
public lemma map_ideal_comap_chart_mul (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    {L : Ideal A} {d : ℕ} {J' : (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).IdealSheafData}
    (hfac : Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d * J' =
      (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)))
    {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
            (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
          (((Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d).comap
            (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal
              ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) *
        Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
            (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
          ((J'.comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom L) :=
  ((map_ideal_comap_mul_top _ _ _ _).symm.trans
      (congrArg (fun K : (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).IdealSheafData =>
        Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
            (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
          ((K.comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩)) hfac)).trans
    ((ideal_comap_chart_eq_map A L ha).trans (map_map_eq _ _ L).symm)

/-- The transported parameters `a = ι x`, `ι y` of a two-dimensional regular local ring `A` span the
maximal ideal of the sections, form a regular sequence, and span the centre's ideal. -/
private lemma chart_parameters_data (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)} (hax : a = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom x) :
    Ideal.span ({a, (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom y} :
        Set Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) ∧
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
      [a, (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom y] ∧
    (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.span ({a, (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom y} :
        Set Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)) := by
  subst hax
  have hspan' := span_pair_inv_eq_maximalIdeal A hspan
  refine ⟨hspan', isRegular_pair_of_span ?_ hspan', centre_ideal_top A x y hspan⟩
  rw [ringKrullDim_sections A, hdim]

/-- **The exceptional divisor of the blowup of a regular local surface at its closed point has a
point.** On the chart `Spec A[𝔪/x]` the exceptional ideal is generated by the image `ξ` of `x`,
and `(ξ)` is a prime ideal of the chart, hence a point of the support. -/
public lemma exists_mem_support_exceptionalIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    ∃ η : Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A),
      η ∈ (Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A)).support := by
  have := isRegularLocalRing_sections A
  obtain ⟨hspan', hreg', hI'⟩ := chart_parameters_data A hdim hspan (y := y) rfl
  have hprime := isPrime_span_algebraMap' hreg' hspan' _ hI'
  have hmem := (mem_support_iff_le ((Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A)).comap
      (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
        (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan)))
      ⟨_, hprime⟩).mpr
    (le_of_eq (ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal A (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan)))
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap] at hmem
  exact ⟨_, hmem⟩

/-- Replacing the left factor of a product of ideals by an equal one, with all ideals behind
variables. -/
private lemma mul_eq_of_eq_left {T : Type u} [CommRing T] {P P' Q S : Ideal T} (h : P = P')
    (h2 : P * Q = S) : P' * Q = S := by rw [← h]; exact h2

/-- Transporting a membership along an equality of ideals, with everything behind variables. -/
private lemma mem_of_eq {T : Type u} [CommRing T] {P Q : Ideal T} {t : T} (h : P = Q)
    (ht : t ∈ Q) : t ∈ P := h ▸ ht

/-- A power of the image of `z` lies in the twice-extended ideal, with all three rings behind
variables. -/
private lemma pow_mem_map_map {R₁ R₂ R₃ : Type u} [CommRing R₁] [CommRing R₂] [CommRing R₃]
    (f : R₂ →+* R₃) (g : R₁ →+* R₂) (K : Ideal R₁) {z : R₁} {w : R₂} (hw : w = g z) {m : ℕ}
    (hz : z ^ m ∈ K) : f w ^ m ∈ Ideal.map f (Ideal.map g K) := by
  subst hw
  rw [← map_pow, ← map_pow]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hz)

/-- Multiplying an ideal inside `(ξ)` by `(ξ ^ d)` lands inside `(ξ ^ (d + 1))`, with everything
behind variables. -/
private lemma mul_le_span_pow_succ {T : Type u} [CommRing T] {ξ : T} {Q : Ideal T} {d : ℕ}
    (hle : Q ≤ Ideal.span {ξ}) : Ideal.span {ξ ^ d} * Q ≤ Ideal.span {ξ ^ (d + 1)} := by
  refine le_trans (Ideal.mul_mono_right hle) (le_of_eq ?_)
  rw [Ideal.span_singleton_mul_span_singleton, ← pow_succ]

/-! ### The support of a residual ideal sheaf on one chart -/

/-- **The part of the support of a residual ideal sheaf lying on one chart.** Let `c` be an open
immersion of the spectrum of a standard chart `Rb[(x, y)/x]` into a scheme `X`, and let `J'` be a
quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on `X` whose ideal `Lc` on that chart contains a power of the image
`ξ` of `x` but is not contained in `(ξ)`. Then the part of the support of `J'` lying on the chart
is finite, each of its points has a local ring of Krull dimension two, and each of them is closed
in the chart.

This is the scheme-theoretic half of [Stacks, Tag 0AGT]: the ring-theoretic input is the
description of the primes above a residual ideal in the sibling module
`CartierDescent.ChartResidualSupport`, and `X` is kept behind a variable so that no blowup has
to be unfolded here. -/
public lemma exists_finite_support_inter_range [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsDomain R] {x y : R}
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R [x, y])
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R) = maximalIdeal R)
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I = Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set R))
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (J' : X.IdealSheafData)
    (c : Spec (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I x)) ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion c] (k : ℕ)
    (hk : algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x ^ k ∈
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I x))).hom.hom
        ((J'.comap c).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩))
    (hnotle : ¬ Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I x))).hom.hom
        ((J'.comap c).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) ≤
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x}) :
    ∃ S : Set X, S.Finite ∧ S = (J'.support : Set X) ∩ Set.range c.base ∧
      ∀ z ∈ S, ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk z) = 2 ∧
        ∀ z', z ⤳ z' → z' ∈ Set.range c.base → z' = z := by
  classical
  set ξ := algebraMap R (affineBlowup I x) x with hξ
  set Lc := Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I x))).hom.hom
    ((J'.comap c).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) with hLc
  have hfinP := finite_setOf_isPrime_le' hreg hspan I hI Lc k hk hnotle
  have hfinW : {w : PrimeSpectrum (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I x)) | Lc ≤ w.asIdeal}.Finite := by
    refine Set.Finite.of_finite_image (f := PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal) (hfinP.subset ?_)
      (fun w _ w' _ h => PrimeSpectrum.ext h)
    rintro p ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨w.isPrime, hw⟩
  refine ⟨c.base '' {w | Lc ≤ w.asIdeal}, hfinW.image _, ?_, ?_⟩
  · ext z
    simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_setOf_eq, Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_range]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨?_, w, rfl⟩
      have h := (mem_support_iff_le (J'.comap c) w).mpr hw
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap, TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_preimage] at h
    · rintro ⟨hz, w, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨w, (mem_support_iff_le (J'.comap c) w).mp ?_, rfl⟩
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap, TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_preimage]
  · rintro z ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
    have hwp := w.isPrime
    have hξw : Ideal.span {ξ} ≤ w.asIdeal := by
      rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
      exact hwp.mem_of_pow_mem k (hw hk)
    have hlt : Ideal.span {ξ} < w.asIdeal :=
      lt_of_le_of_ne hξw fun h => hnotle (by rw [h]; exact hw)
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · refine (ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
        (asIso (Scheme.Hom.stalkMap c w)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv).trans ?_
      refine (ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
        (Spec.stalkIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I x)) w).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv).trans ?_
      exact height_eq_two_of_lt' hreg hspan I hI hwp hlt
    · rintro z' hspec ⟨w', rfl⟩
      have hmaxw : w.asIdeal.IsMaximal :=
        isMaximal_of_isPrime_le' hreg hspan I hI Lc k hk hnotle hwp hw
      have hle : w.asIdeal ≤ w'.asIdeal :=
        (PrimeSpectrum.le_iff_specializes w w').mpr
          (c.isOpenEmbedding.isInducing.specializes_iff.mp hspec)
      exact congrArg c.base (PrimeSpectrum.ext (hmaxw.eq_of_le w'.isPrime.ne_top hle).symm)


/-! ### The residual ideal sheaf is residual on each chart -/

/-- **The chart equation for the residual ideal sheaf.** If `𝒪_X(-dE)·J' = L·𝒪_X`, then on the
chart `Spec A[𝔪/a]` the ideal of `J'` satisfies `(ξ ^ d)·J'(chart) = L·A[𝔪/a]`, where `ξ` is the
image of `a` — the local equation of the exceptional divisor there. -/
public lemma span_pow_mul_ideal_comap_chart (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    {L : Ideal A} {d : ℕ} {J' : (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).IdealSheafData}
    (hfac : Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d * J' =
      (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)))
    {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) :
    Ideal.span {(algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
                  (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ^ d)} *
        Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
            (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
          ((J'.comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom L) :=
  mul_eq_of_eq_left (ideal_comap_chart_exceptionalIdeal_pow A ha d)
    (map_ideal_comap_chart_mul A hfac ha)

/-- **A power of the local equation of the exceptional divisor lies in the residual ideal.** On
the chart `Spec A[𝔪/a]`, the ideal of the cofactor `J'` of `𝒪_X(-dE)` in `L·𝒪_X` contains a power
of the image `ξ` of `a`: the chart equation exhibits `ξ ^ n` in `(ξ ^ d)·J'(chart)`, and `ξ` is a
nonzerodivisor which is not a unit. -/
public lemma exists_pow_mem_ideal_comap_chart (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    {L : Ideal A} {n : ℕ} (hmn : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ n ≤ L)
    {d : ℕ} {J' : (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).IdealSheafData}
    (hfac : Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d * J' =
      (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)))
    {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩)
    (hax : a = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom x) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ^ k ∈
        Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
            (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
          ((J'.comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) := by
  have := isRegularLocalRing_sections A
  have h := chart_parameters_data A hdim hspan (x := x) (y := y) hax
  obtain ⟨hspan', hreg', hI'⟩ := h
  have hxL : x ^ n ∈ L :=
    hmn (Ideal.pow_mem_pow (hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert _ _)) n)
  have hnzd : algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
      (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) :=
    Stacks.Blowup.algebraMap_affineBlowup_mem_nonZeroDivisors _ _
  have hnu := not_isUnit_algebraMap' hreg' hspan' _ hI'
  have hmem : algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
        (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ^ n ∈
      Ideal.span {(algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ^ d)} *
        Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
            (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
          ((J'.comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) :=
    mem_of_eq (span_pow_mul_ideal_comap_chart A hfac ha) (pow_mem_map_map _ _ L hax hxL)
  exact exists_pow_mem_of_pow_mem_span_mul hnzd hnu hmem

/-- **The residual ideal is not contained in the exceptional divisor on any chart.** With `d` the
largest exponent for which `L·𝒪_X ⊆ 𝒪_X(-dE)`, the ideal of the cofactor `J'` on the chart
`Spec A[𝔪/a]` is not contained in `(ξ)`.

This is where the chart-independence of `d` is used: were it contained in `(ξ)` on this one
chart, then `L ⊆ 𝔪 ^ (d + 1)` by
`Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent.le_pow_of_map_le_span_pow`, hence
`L·𝒪_X ⊆ 𝒪_X(-(d+1)E)`, contradicting the maximality of `d`. -/
public lemma not_ideal_comap_chart_le_span (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    {L : Ideal A} {d : ℕ} {J' : (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).IdealSheafData}
    (hfac : Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d * J' =
      (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)))
    (hmax : ¬ ((idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) ≤
      Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ (d + 1)))
    {a : Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ (centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩)
    (hax : a = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom x) :
    ¬ Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of
          (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))).hom.hom
        ((J'.comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
          ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) ≤
      Ideal.span {(algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
        (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a)} := by
  have := isRegularLocalRing_sections A
  have : IsDomain Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain _
  have h := chart_parameters_data A hdim hspan (x := x) (y := y) hax
  obtain ⟨hspan', hreg', hI'⟩ := h
  intro hle
  refine hmax ?_
  have hdvd : Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
        (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a))
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom L) ≤
      Ideal.span {(algebraMap Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤)
        (affineBlowup ((centre A).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) a) a ^ (d + 1))} :=
    (le_of_eq (span_pow_mul_ideal_comap_chart A hfac ha).symm).trans
      (mul_le_span_pow_succ hle)
  have hmapL : Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom L ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) ^ (d + 1) :=
    le_pow_of_map_le_span_pow hreg' hspan' _ hI'
      (ne_zero_of_isSMulRegular (isSMulRegular_of_isRegular hreg')) _ (d + 1) hdvd
  have hcpow : (centre A ^ (d + 1)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) ^ (d + 1) :=
    (congrFun (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow (I := centre A) (d + 1)) _).trans
      (congrArg (· ^ (d + 1)) ((centre_ideal_top_eq_map A).trans (map_inv_maximalIdeal A)))
  have hsheaf : idealSheafOf A L ≤ centre A ^ (d + 1) :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_of_isAffine
      ((idealSheafOf_ideal_top A L).trans_le (hmapL.trans hcpow.ge))
  exact le_trans (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_mono _ hsheaf)
    (le_of_eq (Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_pow (centre A)
      (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) (d + 1)))

/-! ### The finite support of the residual ideal sheaf -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AGT, the finite support assertion.** Let `A` be a two-dimensional
regular local ring with maximal ideal `𝔪 = (x, y)`, let `X` be the blowup of `Spec A` at its
closed point and let `L` be an ideal of `A` with `𝔪 ^ n ⊆ L ⊆ 𝔪`. Then there are a positive
integer `d` and a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf `J'` on `X` with

`𝒪_X(-dE)·J' = L·𝒪_X`,

whose support is contained in a finite set `T` of points of `X`, each of which is closed in `X`
and has a local ring of Krull dimension two. In other words `𝒪_X/J'` is supported in finitely
many closed points of codimension two. -/
public theorem exists_residual_isEffectiveCartier_support (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) {x y : A}
    (hspan : Ideal.span ({x, y} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (L : Ideal A) (n : ℕ) (hmn : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ n ≤ L)
    (hLm : L ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ) (T : Finset (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)))
      (J' : (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).IdealSheafData),
      0 < d ∧
      Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d * J' =
        (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) ∧
      ¬ ((idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) ≤
        Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ (d + 1)) ∧
      ((J'.support : Set (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A))) ⊆ (T : Set _)) ∧
      (∀ z ∈ T, IsClosed ({z} : Set (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)))) ∧
      (∀ z ∈ T, ringKrullDim ((Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A)).presheaf.stalk z) = 2) := by
  classical
  have := isRegularLocalRing_sections A
  have : IsDomain Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of A), ⊤) := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain _
  have hspanyx : Ideal.span ({y, x} : Set A) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := by
    rwa [Set.pair_comm]
  obtain ⟨hspanx, hregx, hIx⟩ := chart_parameters_data A hdim hspan (y := y) rfl
  obtain ⟨hspany, hregy, hIy⟩ := chart_parameters_data A hdim hspanyx (y := x) rfl
  -- the inverse image of `L` lies in the exceptional divisor, and above its `n`-th power
  have hcentre : idealSheafOf A L ≤ centre A :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_of_isAffine
      ((idealSheafOf_ideal_top A L).trans_le
        ((Ideal.map_mono hLm).trans (centre_ideal_top_eq_map A).ge))
  have hJE : (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) ≤
      Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_mono _ hcentre
  have hcn : centre A ^ n ≤ idealSheafOf A L := by
    refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_of_isAffine ?_
    have h1 : (centre A ^ n).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
        Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ n) :=
      (congrFun (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow (I := centre A) n) _).trans
        ((congrArg (· ^ n) (centre_ideal_top_eq_map A)).trans (Ideal.map_pow _ _ n).symm)
    rw [h1, idealSheafOf_ideal_top]
    exact Ideal.map_mono hmn
  have hEn : Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ n ≤
      (idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) :=
    (le_of_eq (Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_pow (centre A)
        (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) n).symm).trans
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_mono _ hcn)
  -- the maximal order `d` along the exceptional divisor, and the cofactor `J'`
  obtain ⟨η, hη⟩ := exists_mem_support_exceptionalIdeal A hdim hspan
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hdmax⟩ := exists_maximal_order (Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A))
    ((idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)))
    (Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal_reesData (centre A)) η hη n hEn
  have hdpos : 0 < d := hdmax 1 (by rw [pow_one]; exact hJE)
  obtain ⟨J', hJ'⟩ := AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mul_eq_of_le_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor
    (Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ d)
    ((idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)))
    (Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_pow
      (Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal_reesData (centre A)) d) hd
  have hmax : ¬ ((idealSheafOf A L).comap (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase (centre A)) ≤
      Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal (centre A) ^ (d + 1)) := by
    intro h
    have := hdmax (d + 1) h
    omega
  -- the residual ideal on each of the two charts
  obtain ⟨kx, hkx⟩ := exists_pow_mem_ideal_comap_chart A hdim hspan hmn hJ'.symm
    (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan) rfl
  obtain ⟨ky, hky⟩ := exists_pow_mem_ideal_comap_chart A hdim hspanyx hmn hJ'.symm
    (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan) rfl
  have hnotlex := not_ideal_comap_chart_le_span A hdim hspan hJ'.symm hmax
    (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan) rfl
  have hnotley := not_ideal_comap_chart_le_span A hdim hspanyx hJ'.symm hmax
    (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan) rfl
  obtain ⟨Sx, hSxfin, hSxeq, hSx⟩ := exists_finite_support_inter_range hregx hspanx _ hIx J'
    (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
      (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan)) kx hkx hnotlex
  obtain ⟨Sy, hSyfin, hSyeq, hSy⟩ := exists_finite_support_inter_range hregy hspany _ hIy J'
    (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
      (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan)) ky hky hnotley
  have hopenx : IsOpen (Set.range (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan)).base) :=
    (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
      (mem_centre_ideal_top_x hspan)).isOpenEmbedding.isOpen_range
  have hopeny : IsOpen (Set.range (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A)
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan)).base) :=
    (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart (centre A) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
      (mem_centre_ideal_top_y hspan)).isOpenEmbedding.isOpen_range
  refine ⟨d, (hSxfin.union hSyfin).toFinset, J', hdpos, hJ'.symm, hmax, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro z hz
    rw [Finset.mem_coe, Set.Finite.mem_toFinset]
    rcases mem_opensRange_chart_or A x y hspan z with hc | hc
    · exact Or.inl (by rw [hSxeq]; exact ⟨hz, hc⟩)
    · exact Or.inr (by rw [hSyeq]; exact ⟨hz, hc⟩)
  · intro z hz
    rw [Set.Finite.mem_toFinset] at hz
    have hzsupp : z ∈ (J'.support : Set (Stacks.Blowup.blowUp (centre A))) := by
      rcases hz with h | h
      · rw [hSxeq] at h
        exact h.1
      · rw [hSyeq] at h
        exact h.1
    rw [← closure_subset_iff_isClosed]
    intro z' hz'
    have hspec : z ⤳ z' := specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hz'
    rcases mem_opensRange_chart_or A x y hspan z' with hc | hc
    · exact (hSx z (by rw [hSxeq]; exact ⟨hzsupp, hspec.mem_open hopenx hc⟩)).2 z' hspec hc
    · exact (hSy z (by rw [hSyeq]; exact ⟨hzsupp, hspec.mem_open hopeny hc⟩)).2 z' hspec hc
  · intro z hz
    rw [Set.Finite.mem_toFinset] at hz
    rcases hz with h | h
    · exact (hSx z h).1
    · exact (hSy z h).1

end Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.CartierDescent

end
